{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791615119,"nonce":"0Zl95FaIYo7C9JHrOhJzqPRMqio=","title":"The typed CFG builder copies every block's statements twice","message":"TypedCfgBuilder::split_statements_in_loop collects a block's statements in `current_statements` (each cloned from the function's typed AST once) and, at each control-flow split, built the block with `statements: current_statements.clone()` before resetting the vector: every statement of every lowered body was deep-cloned a second time, and the copy kept in the vector dropped right after. Clone and drop of typed statements and expressions were about a tenth of lower_program in a Lua nbody start-up profile.\n\nFix: the block takes the vector (std::mem::take); at each of the 18 sites nothing reads `current_statements` before its reset, or the function returns.\n\nStart-up instructions (llvm-backend build, PROFILE_STARTUP=10, median of 3, Mac): Python 9 kernels 48.14G -\u003e 47.87G (-0.56%, every kernel -0.5 to -0.6%); Lua 17 benchmarks 26.37G -\u003e 26.18G (-0.70%); output unchanged.","files":null}]}